  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="345ec2ee-bb0b-5e71-940c-0fba3e87ea21" activityNameId="bbc752f0-14c3-5f95-874d-040e1c08935d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Iron-nickel-chromium alloy, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Iron-nickel-chromium alloy, at plant
Class I nickel as nickel input and ferrochromium (68% Cr) as chromium input used. Scrap is only used as iron bearing input. No nicked or chromium input from the iron scrap assumed.;
Formula: X10NiCrAlTi 32-20; 
Synonyms: Incoloy 800, 1.4876; 
UUID: 684c56ad-b869-333f-8e27-c7f186c6bd3c
Transports of scrap metal and other input materials to electric arc furnace, steel-making process and casting.
Location: Data relate to EAF plants in the EU
Technology: EAV-Process for stainless steel used as approximation for the production of high alloyed iron-nickel-chromium alloys. EU technology mix for electric arc furnace process (mainly furnace with 4th hole, partly with additional evacuation of building atmosphere). 
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: based on literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_684c56ad-b869-333f-8e27-c7f186c6bd3c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
